messages.content:
**Task A: Adaptive Path Scheduling**

Create a new, structured learning path based on the learner's profile.
The number of sessions should be within [1, 10]; if the requested count falls
outside that range, clamp it to the nearest bound.

* **Learner Profile**: {
  "learner_information": "The learner is a marketing analyst with three years of experience in Excel-based reporting and Tableau dashboards, holding a BSc in Business Administration.",
  "learning_goal": "Transition into a junior data scientist role within a year by mastering Python-based data analysis, SQL, and statistics.",
  "cognitive_status": {
    "overall_progress": 15,
    "mastered_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Data Visualization",
        "proficiency_level": "intermediate"
      }
    ],
    "in_progress_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Python Programming",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "SQL",
        "required_proficiency_level": "advanced",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Statistics & Probability",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "unlearned"
      }
    ]
  },
  "learning_preferences": {
    "content_style": "Step-by-step explanations with runnable Python code examples",
    "activity_type": "Hands-on coding exercises on realistic datasets",
    "additional_notes": "Prefers concise summaries before each deep dive and learns best by modifying working code."
  },
  "behavioral_patterns": {
    "system_usage_frequency": "Average of 4 logins per week, mostly on weekday evenings",
    "session_duration_engagement": "Sessions average 35 minutes with sustained engagement on coding exercises",
    "motivational_triggers": "Responds well to progress streaks and milestone badges",
    "additional_notes": "Tends to skim long theory sections and jump ahead to practice tasks."
  }
}
* **Desired Session Count**: 4

text:
{
    "learning_path": [
        {
            "id": "Session 1",
            "title": "Python Essentials for Analysts: From Excel to pandas",
            "abstract": "Quick summary (5 min): Python lets you automate what you currently do in Excel. This session maps familiar spreadsheet concepts to code: cells become variables, ranges become lists, filters become boolean indexing, and pivot tables become groupby(). You'll work step-by-step through runnable code blocks on a realistic marketing campaign dataset, modifying working snippets rather than writing from scratch. Part 1 (15 min): variables, lists, dictionaries, loops, and functions. Part 2 (15 min): load the dataset with pandas, filter rows, select columns, and compute summary metrics like conversion rates. Each exercise is sized for a focused 35-minute sitting with a checkable result at the end. Complete all exercises to earn the 'First Notebook' milestone badge and start your progress streak.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Python Programming"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Python Programming", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 2",
            "title": "SQL for Data Wrangling: Query, Join, and Aggregate",
            "abstract": "Summary first: SQL is how data scientists pull data before analyzing it in Python. You'll learn on a realistic e-commerce database, writing every query yourself in guided, runnable examples. Part 1 (10 min): SELECT, WHERE, and ORDER BY to extract and sort records. Part 2 (15 min): GROUP BY with aggregates (SUM, AVG, COUNT) to build revenue reports, then INNER and LEFT JOIN to combine customer and order tables. Part 3 (10 min): subqueries and window functions (ROW_NUMBER, running totals) for ranking and trend analysis. Finish by connecting to the database from Python using pandas read_sql, bridging directly into your next skill area. Hands-on query challenges come with instant validation to keep your streak alive; passing the join challenges unlocks the 'Query Builder' badge.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["SQL", "Python Programming"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "SQL", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 3",
            "title": "Statistics & Probability in Python: Describe, Test, Decide",
            "abstract": "Concise summary: statistics turns raw data into defensible decisions, the core of a data scientist's job. Theory is kept to short readable blurbs before each coding block, since you learn best by doing. Using numpy and scipy on a marketing A/B test dataset (a domain you already know), you will: compute descriptive statistics and interpret distributions; understand sampling and the central limit theorem through simulation code you can tweak; construct confidence intervals; run t-tests and chi-square tests to compare campaign variants; and measure correlation while distinguishing it from causation. Every concept is introduced in under 3 minutes of reading, then practiced in runnable code you modify and re-run. Sized for a 35-minute session with exercises checkpointed every 10 minutes. Completing the A/B test analysis earns the 'Evidence Decoder' badge.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Statistics & Probability", "Python Programming"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Statistics & Probability", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 4",
            "title": "Capstone: End-to-End Junior Data Scientist Project",
            "abstract": "Summary: this capstone simulates a real junior data scientist take-home task, integrating everything from Sessions 1-3 into one portfolio-ready project. Using a realistic retail dataset, you will: extract and join tables with advanced SQL queries (CTEs and window functions); load results into pandas for cleaning and feature preparation; apply a hypothesis test to validate a business question; and visualize findings with matplotlib and seaborn, extending the dashboard instincts you already have from Tableau. You'll work by modifying a provided working solution scaffold, step-by-step, with each of the four stages fitting a 35-minute session block. The final deliverable is a short insights summary written for business stakeholders, mirroring on-the-job communication. Completing all four stages awards the 'Job-Ready Capstone' badge, a milestone marker for your portfolio and your transition goal.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["SQL", "Python Programming", "Statistics & Probability"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "SQL", "level": "advanced"},
                {"name": "Python Programming", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Statistics & Probability", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        }
    ]
}
